                  "summary": "The spec faithfully translates the PRD's synchronous cancel-exactly-once intent into an observable contract: initial `cancelled` False, state set before release, first cancel returns True with exactly one release call, all later calls return False with no release, exception propagates unchanged while cancellation stays recorded and is never retried, and instances hold independent state. The verification strategy names concrete observations (recording callbacks, state inspection from inside the callback, return values across repeated calls, exception identity plus post-exception assertions, reentrancy, independent instances) and an explicit mutation-kill list (no-op cancel, double callback, state recorded after callback, swallowed exception, retried release, class-level state) that would catch the plausible wrong implementations. Scope files match scope.json (jobs.py, tests/test_jobs.py, README.md) with no new dependencies or architectural change. Repository is otherwise empty, so there are no existing conventions to conform to. No blockers found; two suggestions concern the unspecified README acceptance criterion and a cosmetic mismatch between the spec's stated test command and scope.json's pinned interpreter.",
